Step 1: Pull the Nagios Docker Image
docker pull jasonrivers/nagios:latest

Step 2: Run Nagios
docker run --name nagiosdemo -p 8888:80 jasonrivers/nagios:latest

Step 3: Access Nagios Dashboard
Open browser:
http://localhost:8888
Login Credentials:
Username: nagiosadmin
Password: nagios
Explore:
Hosts – View monitored systems
Services – CPU, memory, processes, etc.
Alerts – Recent notifications

Step 4: Monitoring Host Details
Go to Hosts → select any host
Observe:
Host Status (UP / DOWN)
Metrics (CPU, RAM, Network)
Actions (disable notifications, schedule downtime, etc.)

Step 5: Stop and Remove Nagios
1. Stop the container
docker stop nagiosdemo
2. Remove the container
docker rm nagiosdemo
3. Remove the image (optional)
List images:
docker images
Remove the image:
docker rmi jasonrivers/nagios:latest
4. Observation
In Docker Hub / Dashboard → You can see Nagios container running on port 8888.
